   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** ACE-Step 1.5 XL base (4B) text to music: describe the style, write the lyrics, get a song with vocals as mp3. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Style**: genre, tempo, instruments, the voice, the mix. Full sentences.\n   - **Lyrics**: one line per sung line, with section tags in square brackets: `[Verse 1]`, `[Chorus]`, `[Outro]`. A tag can carry a hint: `[Chorus - Stacked harmonies]`.\n   - **Seconds of music**: length of the song (120 by default).\n   - **BPM**: the tempo (112 by default). Write the same number in **Style**.\n   - **Seed**: a new one every run. Set \"control after generate\" to fixed to keep a song.\n   - **Steps** (50) and **CFG** (6): the template's values.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Prompt**: three settings live on the **Song → conditioning** node (App mode lists them too): **Beats per bar** (4), **Language of the lyrics** (`en`) and **Key** (A major). Change them to fit your song. The other values on that node steer the song planner; they are the template's.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / simple, shift 3, from the official template.\n5. **Save**: press **Run**. The song is decoded in tiles (512 / 64) and the **Result** node saves the mp3 to `output/audio/ACE-Step-1.5/`.\n\n**What to expect:** On the lab card (RTX PRO 4000, 24 GB) with ComfyUI held to about 10 GiB of VRAM: the default 120 s song took 60 s, a 240 s song 122 s, a 60 s instrumental 32 s. An RTX 3060 will be slower; that was not timed. The mp3 is 48 kHz stereo. The song stops a few seconds before the end and the rest is silence (4 s in both samples).\n\n**Tips from the test runs**\n- The default lyrics (two verses, pre-chorus, two choruses) fill 120 s. At 240 s the same lyrics started only after a 90 s intro; at 30 s the song ended after the pre-chorus. Write more or fewer lines when you change the length.\n- For an instrumental, put `[Instrumental]` in **Lyrics** and write \"No vocals\" in **Style**. The 60 s lo-fi sample was made that way.\n- Seeds 1 and 2 with the default text gave two other songs with the same lyrics sung.\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3, RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 64 GB RAM, 2026-11-22. Checked by transcription and spectrogram, not by ear. Not run on a real 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
